  <section xml:id="grading">
    <title>Course Requirements and Grading</title>
    <!--Edit this example as necessary for your course.-->
    <p>
      Final grades will be determined using the following assignment categories (descriptions below):
    </p>
    <tabular>
      <row header="yes">
        <cell>Assignment Category</cell> <cell>Weight</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>Homework</cell> <cell>50%</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>Class Participation</cell> <cell>15%</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>Term Project</cell> <cell>30% each</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>Reflection Essay</cell> <cell>5%</cell>
      </row>
    </tabular>
    <p>
      Grading Scale
    </p>
    <tabular>
      <row header="yes">
        <cell>Letter Grade</cell><cell>Point Range (<m>P</m>)</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>A </cell><cell><m>P &gt;93</m></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>A-</cell><cell><m>90\leq P &lt; 93</m></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>B+</cell><cell><m>87\leq P &lt; 90</m></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>B</cell><cell><m>83\leq P &lt; 87</m></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>B-</cell><cell><m>80\leq P &lt; 83</m></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>C+</cell><cell><m>77\leq P &lt; 80</m></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>C</cell><cell><m>83\leq P &lt; 87</m></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>C-</cell><cell><m>70\leq P &lt; 73</m></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>D+</cell><cell><m>67\leq P &lt; 70</m></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>D</cell><cell><m>63\leq P &lt; 67</m></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>D-</cell><cell><m>60\leq P &lt; 63</m></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>F</cell><cell><m> P &lt; 60</m></cell>
      </row>
    </tabular>

  
  <paragraphs xml:id="homework">
    <title>Homework</title>
    <p>
    Homework will be assigned (almost) daily. It will consist of problems related to the material we are discussing. Typically, each day's assigned homework will be due, on Canvas, on the day of the next class period. In some cases, a more significant assignment will be given (a "mini-project"). For those, the main deliverable will be an in-class presentation which will be graded with a rubric given at the time of the assignment.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
  <paragraphs xml:id="participation">
    <title>Class Participation</title>
    <p>
      An important part of history is a discussion of the actual history and how it relates to our own experience. Given this, attendance is mandatory and a participation grade will be given daily.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
  <paragraphs xml:id="term-project">
    <title>Term Project</title>
    <p>
      Each student will complete a term project about some piece of the history of mathematics. Details will be given in the coming weeks. Oral presentations will be given the last week of class.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
  <paragraphs xml:id="reflection">
    <title>Reflection Essay</title>
    <p>
      In lieu of a final exam, you will be asked to write a reflection paper and participate in a class discussion during the final exam period.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
</section>